{
  "id": "about-the-author",
  "kind": "epilogue",
  "sourceKind": "about-author",
  "label": "About the Author",
  "title": "ABOUT THE AUTHOR",
  "shortTitle": "ABOUT THE AUTHOR",
  "sourceRange": [
    713,
    737
  ],
  "headerSourceParagraphs": {
    "title": 713
  },
  "elements": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Lalit R. Mishra is the creator of The Human Fiction series."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 714
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "His work does not come from academic philosophy or structured theory…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 715
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "but from observation of everyday experience — thought, identity, interpretation, and the quiet mechanisms behind them."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 716
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He is interested in one recurring question:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 717
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "why does life feel like it is happening to a “someone” inside experience?"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 718
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Rather than offering answers, his writing focuses on exposing patterns:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 719
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "how the mind constructs continuity,"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 720
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "how meaning attaches itself to events,"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 721
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "how identity forms through memory and narration,"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 722
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "and how a stable sense of “I” emerges without ever being directly found."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 723
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "His approach is not to convince or conclude…"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 724
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "but to observe carefully enough that assumptions begin to lose their automatic strength."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 725
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "In his view, clarity is not something added to life."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 726
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It is what remains when unnecessary interpretation slows down."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 727
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The Human Fiction series reflects this inquiry:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 728
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "not as a belief system,"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 729
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "not as a philosophy to follow,"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 730
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "but as a structured exploration of how human experience becomes personal through narration."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 731
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He does not claim authority over truth."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 732
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "He only points toward the structure through which truth is usually interpreted."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 733
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "And within that structure, one question remains central:"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 734
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "if experience is happening, where exactly is the “one” it is happening to?"
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 735
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "This question is not meant to be answered."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 736
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "It is meant to be seen clearly enough that its urgency dissolves on its own."
        }
      ],
      "sourceParagraph": 737
    }
  ],
  "index": 22,
  "suppressHeaderNumber": true,
  "file": "chapters/22-about-the-author.json"
}
